\label{lemma:earlyhit}
Let $M$ be an $n \times \ell$ matrix whose elements are taken from a finite set $S$ of size $|S|=s$, let $A$ be a set, and let $P \geq 0$ be a penalty. Let $hit(M_i, A)$ be the index of the first element of $M_i$, the $i$-th row of $M$, that belongs to $A$, or $\ell+P$, if no element of $M_i$ belongs to $A$. Let $hit(M, A) = \sum_{i=1}^{n} hit(M_i, A)$ be the \text{hitting sum} of $A$ with respect to $M$.

Then, for every $0 < p < 1$ there is an $O(n\ell)$ time algorithm which finds a set $A \subseteq S$ for which $\frac{n}{p^2s}|A|+hit(M, A) \leq 3n/p + (1-p)^\ell Pn$.

