\label{fact:monotonicitydistance}
For quantum states $\rho_A$, $\sigma_A \in \D(A)$, and a quantum operation $\E(\cdot):\L(A)\rightarrow \L(B)$, it holds that
\begin{align*}
	\Delta(\E(\rho_A) , \E(\sigma_A)) \leq \Delta(\rho_A,\sigma_A) \quad \mbox{and} \quad \BR(\E(\rho_A),\E(\sigma_A)) \leq \BR(\rho_A,\sigma_A),
\end{align*}
with equality if $\E$ is unitary. 
In particular, for bipartite states $\rho_{AB},\sigma_{AB}\in \D(AB)$, it holds that
\begin{align*}
	\Delta(\rho_{AB},\sigma_{AB}) \geq \Delta(\rho_A,\sigma_A) \quad \mbox{and} \quad \BR(\rho_{AB},\sigma_{AB}) \geq \BR(\rho_A,\sigma_A).
\end{align*}

