\label{th:main-inf}
    Let $L = (L_\mathrm{yes},L_\mathrm{no})$ be a promise language in $\QMA$, and $x \in \{0,1\}^n$ be an input for the language $L$. Let $U_x$ be a verification circuit acting on $N$ qubits and $T$ be the number of elementary gates of $U_x$. Then, for any integer $d\geq1$, there exists a $(d+1)$-local Hamiltonian $H_x$ acting on $N + O(T^{1/d})$ qubits satisfying the following properties;
